From 9f0ddbb8943fc12cae5e052f0f4b9188de6e4af9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 11:41:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] soc: apple: opt into reserved DRAM AOP ring discovery

The early capture skipped 525762560 reserved bytes. An inherited
AFK ring can be hidden by Linux's crash-kernel, CMA or other DRAM
reservations, even when their original contents survived boot.

Add immutable ring_scan_reserved=1 for E1. Relax only the memblock
and PageReserved exclusion; require valid linear-mapped, full-page
memblock RAM backed by System RAM resources. Keep no-map, MMIO,
self/stack and fault quarantine exclusions unconditional. The flag
is captured before the postcore scan and defaults off. No mapping,
permission, reservation, shared-memory write or AOP traffic is added.

Label each hit with PA and its captured range class: system-ram,
crash-kernel, cma, reserved-dram or mixed. Use kernel crash-resource
descriptors and CMA membership, including discontiguous CMA areas;
never infer addresses from a boot log. Labels do not prove untouched
contents. Keep coverage/skipped-reason reporting and E2 unchanged.

Host ASan/UBSan tests compile the production policy, classifier and
scan loop: default/opt-in reserved behavior, mixed hits, no-map crash
ranges, invalid PFNs/maps, non-RAM resources, self exclusion, AOP
firmware-window refusal and fault quarantine. No device access.

Signed-off-by: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
---
 Documentation/driver-api/apple-a9-aop.rst | 31 ++++++++++--
 drivers/soc/apple/Kconfig                 |  2 +
 drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop-ring-reader.c    | 61 ++++++++++++++++++++---
 drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop-ring.h           |  8 +++
 drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop.h                |  2 +
 drivers/soc/apple/apple-a9-aop.c          |  8 +++
 6 files changed, 103 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/driver-api/apple-a9-aop.rst b/Documentation/driver-api/apple-a9-aop.rst
index 6c99f6054b..2bffdda986 100644
--- a/Documentation/driver-api/apple-a9-aop.rst
+++ b/Documentation/driver-api/apple-a9-aop.rst
@@ -362,8 +362,9 @@ E1: reading the root-only ``/sys/kernel/debug/apple-a9-aop/ring_scan`` performs
 one scan per boot and freezes the result. Subsequent reads and seq_file buffer
 retries only format the saved result. It inventories full pages in memblock
 RAM, including no-map ranges for coverage, but only reads pages proven to be
-System RAM by the resource tree. It explicitly skips memblock reservations,
-PageReserved, no-map and invalid linear-map pages. Readable pages require
+System RAM by the resource tree. By default it skips memblock reservations
+and PageReserved pages; no-map and invalid linear-map pages are always skipped.
+Readable pages require
 pfn_valid, pfn_is_map_memory and virt_addr_valid before page-confined
 copy_from_kernel_nofault through phys_to_virt. No /dev/mem, guessed MMIO,
 ioremap, page reference, allocator lock or cache clean/invalidate is used.
@@ -400,6 +401,29 @@ same-reason pages, and explicitly counts omitted bytes if that storage fills.
 Coverage counters and PFN quarantine remain exact even then. Tracking is
 bounded to a 4 GiB DRAM address span; a larger span refuses allocation.
 
+Optional ``apple_a9_aop.ring_scan_reserved=1`` requires debug=1 and ring_scan=1.
+It also admits reserved linear-mapped DRAM, including crash-kernel, CMA and
+other memblock/PageReserved reservations, after the same full-page memblock
+RAM, System RAM resource, pfn_valid, pfn_is_map_memory and virt_addr_valid
+checks. No-map, MMIO, reader/stack exclusions and fault quarantine remain
+unconditional. No mapping, reservation or permission is changed. In particular,
+the AOP firmware window at 0x210e00000 is not DRAM and is never added to E1.
+This modifier works with either lazy or postcore capture, and its effective
+value is frozen into ``ring_scan_reserved`` in the report. Coverage counters
+and skipped-reason/range reporting retain their existing meanings.
+
+Every hit reports its PA and ``range_class``: system-ram, crash-kernel, cma,
+reserved-dram or mixed. Crash-kernel membership uses IORES_DESC_CRASH_KERNEL;
+CMA membership uses the kernel CMA-area iterator and cma_intersects, including
+discontiguous areas. Other reserved membership uses memblock/PageReserved.
+These are metadata labels, not guessed address windows. A ring covering
+different page classes is mixed. Labels are captured at discovery and do not
+establish that Linux never wrote the bytes: CMA can have consumers and the
+kernel/boot-payload reservation has already been overwritten. An advancing
+pointer and valid 0xc2 payload remain required to identify a live accel ring.
+E2's separate plain no-map reservation contract is unchanged; a hit in a
+crash-kernel or CMA region does not authorize its automatic reuse by E2.
+
 Optional ``apple_a9_aop.ring_scan_early=1`` requires debug=1 and ring_scan=1.
 It runs the same one-shot scan/watch at postcore_initcall_sync, after memory
 management/scheduling and the arm64 RAM resource map exist, before platform
@@ -409,7 +433,8 @@ scan, even on early failure. The phase is ``postcore-initcall`` (or
 ``early-unavailable`` on failure); the default is ``debugfs``. An early scan
 can delay boot by up to about 47 seconds. It still occurs after Linux's initial
 allocations, and on a warm kexec the previous kernel already reused RAM.
-For the best cold-boot evidence, put all three flags in the FIRST Linux boot
+For the best cold-boot evidence, put debug=1, ring_scan=1, ring_scan_early=1
+and, when requested, ring_scan_reserved=1 in the FIRST Linux boot
 after iOS -> DFU -> Linux, without an intervening Linux or AON power cycle.
 
 A late debugfs scan cannot establish that pages were never allocated. Output
diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/apple/Kconfig
index edd4256168..1dc169f2bd 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/Kconfig
@@ -20,6 +20,8 @@ config APPLE_A9_AOP
 	  With debug=1 ring_scan=1, ring_scan_early=1 captures at postcore initcall
 	  before device probing. E1 skips protected/unreadable pages and reports
 	  bounded coverage; it never reserves or writes the inherited rings.
+	  ring_scan_reserved=1 also reads reserved linear-mapped System RAM;
+	  no-map pages and MMIO remain excluded.
 
 config APPLE_A9_AOP_IIO
 	bool "J71t AOP accelerometer IIO consumer"
diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop-ring-reader.c b/drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop-ring-reader.c
index f6971f140b..3dbfb9ed86 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop-ring-reader.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/a9-aop-ring-reader.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
  * IIO only uses an early DT no-map RAM reservation with a RO WB mapping.
  */
 #include <linux/bitmap.h>
+#include <linux/cma.h>
 #include <linux/debugfs.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/iio/iio.h>
@@ -40,6 +41,7 @@
 
 struct rr_hit {
 	phys_addr_t pa;
+	enum a9_rr_range_class range_class;
 	struct a9_rr_header first;
 	struct a9_rr_header last;
 	struct a9_rr_report report;
@@ -75,6 +77,7 @@ struct a9_ring_reader {
 	unsigned int nr_hits;
 	int scan_errno;
 	bool scan_done;
+	bool scan_reserved;
 	const char *scan_stop;
 	phys_addr_t fault_pa;
 	phys_addr_t scan_fault_pa;
@@ -127,13 +130,14 @@ static int rr_scan_page_reason(struct a9_ring_reader *rr, phys_addr_t pa)
 		return A9_RR_SKIP_INVALID; /* Already accounted; never retry. */
 	if (!pfn_is_map_memory(PHYS_PFN(pa)))
 		return A9_RR_SKIP_NOMAP;
-	if (memblock_is_region_reserved(pa, PAGE_SIZE))
+	if (!rr->scan_reserved && memblock_is_region_reserved(pa, PAGE_SIZE))
 		return A9_RR_SKIP_RESERVED;
 	if (!rr_linear_page(pa))
 		return A9_RR_SKIP_INVALID;
-	if (PageReserved(pfn_to_page(PHYS_PFN(pa))))
+	if (!rr->scan_reserved && PageReserved(pfn_to_page(PHYS_PFN(pa))))
 		return A9_RR_SKIP_RESERVED;
-	if (region_intersects(pa, PAGE_SIZE, IORESOURCE_SYSTEM_RAM | IORESOURCE_BUSY,
+	if (!memblock_is_region_memory(pa, PAGE_SIZE) ||
+	    region_intersects(pa, PAGE_SIZE, IORESOURCE_SYSTEM_RAM | IORESOURCE_BUSY,
 			      IORES_DESC_NONE) != REGION_INTERSECTS)
 		return A9_RR_SKIP_RESOURCE;
 	/* Never rediscover our own copied headers as apparent live DMA rings. */
@@ -152,6 +156,43 @@ static int rr_scan_page_reason(struct a9_ring_reader *rr, phys_addr_t pa)
 	return -1;
 }
 
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CMA)
+static int rr_cma_page(struct cma *cma, void *data)
+{
+	phys_addr_t pa = *(phys_addr_t *)data;
+
+	/* This also handles discontiguous CMA areas, without cma_get_base(). */
+	return cma_intersects(cma, pa, pa + PAGE_SIZE - 1);
+}
+#endif
+
+/* Informational membership, not a claim that the bytes were never written. */
+static enum a9_rr_range_class rr_page_class(phys_addr_t pa)
+{
+	if (region_intersects(pa, PAGE_SIZE, IORESOURCE_MEM,
+			      IORES_DESC_CRASH_KERNEL) == REGION_INTERSECTS)
+		return A9_RR_CLASS_CRASH;
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_CMA)
+	if (cma_for_each_area(rr_cma_page, &pa))
+		return A9_RR_CLASS_CMA;
+#endif
+	if (memblock_is_region_reserved(pa, PAGE_SIZE) ||
+	    PageReserved(pfn_to_page(PHYS_PFN(pa))))
+		return A9_RR_CLASS_RESERVED;
+	return A9_RR_CLASS_RAM;
+}
+
+static enum a9_rr_range_class rr_hit_class(phys_addr_t pa)
+{
+	phys_addr_t page = round_down(pa, PAGE_SIZE);
+	enum a9_rr_range_class class = rr_page_class(page);
+
+	for (page += PAGE_SIZE; page < pa + A9_RR_SIZE; page += PAGE_SIZE)
+		if (rr_page_class(page) != class)
+			return A9_RR_CLASS_MIXED;
+	return class;
+}
+
 static void rr_skip_page(struct a9_ring_reader *rr, phys_addr_t pa,
 			 enum a9_rr_skip_reason reason)
 {
@@ -317,6 +358,7 @@ static int rr_scan_range(struct resource *res, void *data)
 				continue;
 			hit = &rr->hits[rr->nr_hits++];
 			hit->pa = pa + offset;
+			hit->range_class = rr_hit_class(hit->pa);
 			hit->first = header;
 			hit->last = header;
 			memcpy(hit->prefix, rr->snapshot, sizeof(hit->prefix));
@@ -430,6 +472,9 @@ static int rr_scan_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 		"no-map", "reserved", "not-system-ram", "invalid-linear-map",
 		"reader-or-stack", "read-fault",
 	};
+	static const char * const classes[] = {
+		"system-ram", "crash-kernel", "cma", "reserved-dram", "mixed",
+	};
 	u64 unvisited;
 
 	if (mutex_lock_interruptible(&rr->lock))
@@ -440,6 +485,8 @@ static int rr_scan_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 	seq_puts(s, "format=2 hardware_writes=none mailbox=none rptr_writes=none frozen=1\n");
 	seq_puts(s, "ownership=lockless-current-state historical_allocation=unknown cache_coherency=unverified\n");
 	seq_puts(s, "excluded=reader-allocations-and-current-kernel-stack\n");
+	seq_printf(s, "ring_scan_reserved=%u class_source=kernel-resource-and-cma-metadata\n",
+		   rr->scan_reserved);
 	seq_printf(s, "scan_stop=%s errno=%d bytes=%llu skipped=%llu hits=%u elapsed_ms=%llu fault_pa=%pa\n",
 		   rr->scan_stop, rr->scan_errno, c->scanned, c->skipped, rr->nr_hits,
 		   div_u64(rr->scan_end_ns - rr->scan_start_ns, NSEC_PER_MSEC), &rr->scan_fault_pa);
@@ -457,9 +504,10 @@ static int rr_scan_show(struct seq_file *s, void *unused)
 			   c->ranges[i].end - c->ranges[i].start);
 	for (i = 0; i < rr->nr_hits; i++) {
 		hit = &rr->hits[i];
-		seq_printf(s, "hit=%u pa=%pa bufsize=0x%x marker=0x%x rptr=0x%x wptr_discovery=0x%x wptr_watch_first=0x%x wptr_last=0x%x changes=%u advanced=%s watch_ms=%llu\n",
-			   i, &hit->pa, hit->first.bufsize, hit->first.marker,
-			   hit->last.rptr, hit->first.wptr, hit->watch_wptr,
+		seq_printf(s, "hit=%u pa=%pa range_class=%s bufsize=0x%x marker=0x%x rptr=0x%x wptr_discovery=0x%x wptr_watch_first=0x%x wptr_last=0x%x changes=%u advanced=%s watch_ms=%llu\n",
+			   i, &hit->pa, classes[hit->range_class],
+			   hit->first.bufsize, hit->first.marker, hit->last.rptr,
+			   hit->first.wptr, hit->watch_wptr,
 			   hit->last.wptr, hit->changes,
 			   hit->changes ? "yes" : "no",
 			   hit->last_ns ? div_u64(hit->last_ns - hit->watch_ns,
@@ -808,6 +856,7 @@ static struct a9_ring_reader *rr_alloc(void)
 		return ERR_PTR(-ENOMEM);
 	mutex_init(&rr->lock);
 	rr->scan_phase = "debugfs";
+	rr->scan_reserved = apple_a9_aop_ring_scan_reserved();
 	if (end <= start || end - start > RR_MAX_SPAN) {
 		ret = -ERANGE;
 		goto fail;
